"-- codec.st: PBCodec, the canonical values of format 4 --

The wire form of a value is the msgpack data of the ProtoBase format spec
(v2.0.0rc2, 'Canonical values'). PBCodec turns a protoST value into that data
and back, with every refusal of the spec:

  PBCodec canonical: aValue              the canonical value, or PBValidationError
  PBCodec toWire: aValue atomRef: aBlock a tree MessagePack encode: takes
  PBCodec fromWire: aTree resolver: r    a value, or PBCorruptionError
  PBCodec encode: aValue                 the msgpack bytes of one value
  PBCodec decode: aByteArray             one value from its bytes

Kinds (format kind: protoST class):
  nil, bool: nil, true, false        int: Integer (@int outside -2^63..2^64-1)
  float: Float                       str: String         bytes: ByteArray
  decimal: Decimal (@dec)            date: CalendarDate (@date)
  time: TimeOfDay (@time)            datetime: DateTime (@dt)
  timedelta: TimeSpan (@td)          uuid: UUID (@uuid)
  list: PBFrozenList (an Array or an OrderedCollection is copied)
  tuple: PBTuple (@tup)              map: PBFrozenDict (@map)
  missing: PBMissing default         mutable: PBMutableObject (@mut)
  ref: an atom (anything answering isPBReference: PBAtom, PBUnresolvedRef),
       through the atomRef: block; a @ref is read with the tag a writer puts
       (PBTypeRegistry canonicalTag:): a built-in name becomes its alias, an
       application alias the declared name of its registered class

Refused when written (PBValidationError naming the class): a Symbol (the @sym
kind is reserved and not in format 4, Spec 4.4), a Fraction, a Character, a
Dictionary (its order is unspecified, and the order is part of the bytes: use
PBFrozenDict), a Set, a Bag, an Interval, a block, a class, and any other
object. A host subclass of a mapped class is stored as its base value, read
from the base class's instance variables, never through the subclass's
methods.

Time zones (design 4.3). There is no time-zone database. A zone key is known
when it is in PBZoneKeys, the pinned key list of one IANA tzdata release
(zonekeys.st, generated by tools/gen_zone_keys.py); an unknown key is
PBValidationError when written and PBCorruptionError when read, on every
machine. An instant-form datetime is read as its UTC instant and its key, as
the format spec lets a reader without a database present it; whether its wall
clock in the zone stays within years 1 to 9999 is not checked when reading.
Writing one within a day of either end is refused with PBNotSupportedError,
since ProtoBase would refuse to read it back if the wall clock fell outside.
A format-3 ['zone', key] datetime is read as a PBLegacyZoneDateTime and is
never written.

Strings: every string the codec writes (a value, a map key, a fixed zone's
name, a mutable name, a reference's type name) is checked: one holding a lone
surrogate (16rD800..16rDFFF) is not valid UTF-8 and is refused with
PBValidationError (format spec, Known gaps). Zone keys are ASCII by the
pinned list.

Nesting (format spec v2.0.0rc2, 'Value nesting depth'; ProtoBase D60): the
wire form of a value nests at most PBCodec maxValueDepth = 1022 msgpack
containers (MAX_VALUE_DEPTH), counted from the value itself: a list adds 1, a
tuple 2 ({'@tup': [...]}), a map 3 ({'@map': [[k, v], ...]}, 2 when empty),
@int, @dec, @uuid, @missing and @mut 1, @date, @td, @ref and a naive @time or
@dt 2, an aware @time or @dt 3; an empty container counts like any other, and
map keys are on the paths. A deeper value is refused when it is made
canonical (PBValidationError) and deeper data when it is read
(PBCorruptionError), at the same count; inside an atom record a value sits two
containers deep, so a record holds at most 1024, what protoST's MessagePack
(and msgpack-python from 1.2.0) packs and unpacks. The three depth refusals
are ProtoBase's text word for word (values.too_deep_error, check_wrapped and
codec._too_deep_data), without the 'PBCodec: ' prefix of the codec's other
messages, so one database refuses one value with one sentence in both
languages; only a holder naming a collection class differs ('PBList element',
where ProtoBase says 'List element'). A record deeper than 1024 is refused by
protoST's MessagePack (MessagePackDepthExceeded) before the codec sees it:
PBCorruptionError with ProtoBase's storage.format.undecodable_atom sentence,
'Undecodable atom at AtomPointer(...): it nests deeper than 1024 MessagePack
containers, so a value in it nests deeper than MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = 1022 ...'
(tooDeepData:).

  PBCodec tooDeepData: aWhat                  the PBCorruptionError of a record
                                              deeper than 1024 containers
  PBCodec canonical: aValue for: aHolder      canonical:, a PBValidationError
                                              of its own naming aHolder
  PBCodec check: v wrapping: n holder: h wrapper: w
                                              PBValidationError when n
                                              containers a structure stores
                                              around v pass the limit
  PBCodec valueDepth: aValue                  the containers v's wire form nests

Every walk of a value (canonical:, the wire form, fromWire:resolver:,
valueDepth:) uses an explicit stack, never recursion: protoST bounds a
recursion through do: or collect: at about 1,000 levels, and a worker thread
must read what the main thread writes.

Decoding checks the tree that MessagePack decodeOrdered: answers: map keys are
strings, no ext value, exactly one key per tagged map, one spelling for @int,
@dec, @td and the date and time fields. Every map is written as a
MessagePackMap, so the bytes keep their order."

Import from: 'protobase/errors'.
Import from: 'protobase/values'.
Import from: 'protobase/keys'.
Import from: 'decimal'.
Import from: 'calendar'.
Import from: 'protobase/zonekeys'.
Import from: 'protobase/registry'.
Import from: 'uuid'.

Object subclass: #PBCodec.

"=== constants ================================================================"

PBCodec class >> _intMin
  ^ -9223372036854775808.

PBCodec class >> _intMax
  ^ 18446744073709551615.

"CPython's decimal limits on a string it converts (MIN_ETINY and MAX_EMAX):
 the exponent of a finite decimal, and its adjusted exponent."
PBCodec class >> _decimalMinExponent
  ^ -1999999999999999997.

PBCodec class >> _decimalMaxAdjusted
  ^ 999999999999999999.

"MAX_VALUE_DEPTH: the most msgpack containers the wire form of a stored value
 nests, counted from the value (format spec, 'Value nesting depth')."
PBCodec class >> maxValueDepth
  ^ 1022.

"The ordinal microseconds within which every wall clock of an instant lies in
 years 1 to 9999, whatever its zone's offset (|offset| < 24 h)."
PBCodec class >> _instantLow
  ^ 86399999999.

PBCodec class >> _instantHigh
  ^ 315537897599999999 - 86399999999.

"=== canonical values ========================================================="

"aValue in canonical form: containers frozen (an Array or OrderedCollection
 becomes a PBFrozenList), host subclasses reduced to their base values. An
 already canonical value is answered as is. A value that cannot be stored
 signals PBValidationError naming its class, and so does one nested deeper
 than maxValueDepth containers."
PBCodec class >> canonical: aValue
  | stack result |
  result := self _canonicalOpen: aValue depth: 0 on: nil.
  (result isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [^ result].
  stack := OrderedCollection with: result.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | frame r |
    frame := stack last.
    frame atEnd
      ifTrue: [
        stack removeLast.
        r := self _canonicalClose: frame]
      ifFalse: [r := self _canonicalOpen: frame next depth: frame depth on: stack].
    (r isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [
      stack isEmpty ifTrue: [result := r] ifFalse: [stack last add: r]]].
  ^ result.

"Python's repr of the String aString, for the texts that quote a name as
 ProtoBase's messages do (a holder such as Root 'name', Python f'{name!r}'):
 single quotes, or double quotes when aString holds a single quote and no
 double one; a backslash and the chosen quote escaped; tab, newline and
 carriage return as \t, \n and \r; the other code points below U+0100
 that Python does not print (C0 and C1 controls, DEL, U+00A0 and U+00AD) as
 \xhh. Code points from U+0100 up are kept as they are: Python also escapes
 the ones its unicodedata calls non-printable (separators, format characters,
 private use, unassigned), a table protoST does not carry, so only those
 differ."
PBCodec class >> repr: aString
  | quote out |
  quote := ((aString includes: $') and: [(aString includes: $") not]) ifTrue: [$"] ifFalse: [$'].
  out := WriteStream on: String new.
  out nextPut: quote.
  aString do: [:ch |
    | cp hex |
    cp := ch asInteger.
    (ch = quote or: [ch = $\])
      ifTrue: [out nextPut: $\; nextPut: ch]
      ifFalse: [
        cp = 9 ifTrue: [out nextPutAll: '\t'] ifFalse: [
        cp = 10 ifTrue: [out nextPutAll: '\n'] ifFalse: [
        cp = 13 ifTrue: [out nextPutAll: '\r'] ifFalse: [
        ((cp < 32 or: [cp between: 127 and: 160]) or: [cp = 173])
          ifTrue: [
            hex := (cp printString: 16) asLowercase.
            out nextPutAll: '\x'; nextPutAll: (hex size = 1 ifTrue: ['0' , hex] ifFalse: [hex])]
          ifFalse: [out nextPut: ch]]]]]].
  out nextPut: quote.
  ^ out contents.

"As canonical:, with a PBValidationError of the codec's own (not of a subclass)
 signalled again with aHolder in front: the field, root, mutable cell or
 collection element the value was going to (ProtoBase canonical_for). aHolder
 is a String, or a block answering one, evaluated only when the value is
 refused: the callers on the write path pass a block, so the text is built on
 the error path only."
PBCodec class >> canonical: aValue for: aHolder
  ^ [self canonical: aValue] on: PBValidationError do: [:e |
    e class == PBValidationError ifFalse: [e pass].
    PBValidationError signal: (aHolder isString ifTrue: [aHolder] ifFalse: [aHolder value]) , ': ' , e messageText].

"The msgpack containers the wire form of the canonical value aValue nests
 (format spec, 'Value nesting depth'), counted with an explicit stack."
PBCodec class >> valueDepth: aValue
  | stack best |
  best := 0.
  stack := OrderedCollection with: aValue -> 0.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | entry v d items |
    entry := stack removeLast.
    v := entry key.
    d := entry value.
    items := nil.
    (v isClassObject not and: [v isKindOf: _PBSequence])
      ifTrue: [
        d := d + ((v isKindOf: PBTuple) ifTrue: [2] ifFalse: [1]).
        items := self _field: 'items' of: v base: _PBSequence]
      ifFalse: [(v isClassObject not and: [v isKindOf: PBFrozenDict])
        ifTrue: [
          (self _field: 'keys' of: v base: PBFrozenDict) isEmpty
            ifTrue: [d := d + 2]
            ifFalse: [
              d := d + 3.
              items := (self _field: 'keys' of: v base: PBFrozenDict) , (self _field: 'values' of: v base: PBFrozenDict)]]
        ifFalse: [d := d + (self _leafContainers: v)]].
    d > best ifTrue: [best := d].
    items isNil ifFalse: [1 to: items size do: [:i | stack addLast: (items at: i) -> d]]].
  ^ best.

"Signals PBValidationError when anInteger containers that a structure stores
 around the canonical value aValue (aWrapper: 'its bucket tuple') would make
 the stored attribute value nest deeper than maxValueDepth; aHolder names the
 value ('PBSet element'). A scalar nests at most 3 containers, so only a
 container is walked (ProtoBase check_wrapped)."
PBCodec class >> check: aValue wrapping: anInteger holder: aHolder wrapper: aWrapper
  | limit depth |
  limit := self maxValueDepth - anInteger.
  (aValue isClassObject not and: [(aValue isKindOf: _PBSequence) or: [aValue isKindOf: PBFrozenDict]]) ifFalse: [^ aValue].
  depth := self valueDepth: aValue.
  depth > limit ifTrue: [
    ^ PBValidationError signal: aHolder , ' nests ' , depth printString , ' MessagePack containers deep, and '
      , aWrapper , ' adds ' , anInteger printString , ' around it, so it may nest at most ' , limit printString
      , ' (MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = ' , self maxValueDepth printString , ', format spec "Value nesting depth")'].
  ^ aValue.

PBCodec class >> _tooDeep
  ^ PBValidationError signal: 'The value nests deeper than MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = '
    , self maxValueDepth printString
    , ' MessagePack containers, the most the storage format allows (format spec, "Value nesting depth")'.

"The PBCorruptionError of msgpack data deeper than a record may nest
 (protoST's MessagePack refuses it with MessagePackDepthExceeded), after
 aWhat, in the words of ProtoBase's storage.format.undecodable_atom: an atom
 payload nests two containers (its envelope and its state map) above its
 attribute values, so a record deeper than 1024 holds a value deeper than
 MAX_VALUE_DEPTH. For an atom record aWhat is 'Undecodable atom at
 <PBAtomPointer pythonText>', ProtoBase's whole sentence."
PBCodec class >> tooDeepData: aWhat
  ^ PBCorruptionError signal: aWhat , ': it nests deeper than 1024 MessagePack containers, so a value in it nests deeper than MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = '
    , self maxValueDepth printString , ' (format spec, "Value nesting depth")'.

PBCodec class >> _tooDeepData
  ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'The encoded value nests deeper than MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = '
    , self maxValueDepth printString
    , ' MessagePack containers, the most the storage format allows (format spec, "Value nesting depth")'.

"The msgpack containers the wire form of the canonical scalar v nests: 0 for a
 value written natively, 1 for a tag whose body is a scalar (@int, @dec,
 @uuid, @missing, @mut), 2 for a tag whose body is an array of scalars
 (@date, @td, @ref, a naive @time or @dt), 3 for an aware @time or @dt (its
 time zone, or its instant form, is an array inside the body)."
PBCodec class >> _leafContainers: v
  v isNil ifTrue: [^ 0].
  (v == true or: [v == false]) ifTrue: [^ 0].
  v isInteger ifTrue: [^ (v between: self _intMin and: self _intMax) ifTrue: [0] ifFalse: [1]].
  (v isFloat or: [v isString or: [v isKindOf: ByteArray]]) ifTrue: [^ 0].
  ((v isKindOf: DateTime) or: [v isKindOf: TimeOfDay]) ifTrue: [^ v zone isNil ifTrue: [2] ifFalse: [3]].
  ((v isKindOf: CalendarDate) or: [v isKindOf: TimeSpan]) ifTrue: [^ 2].
  (self _isReference: v) ifTrue: [^ 2].
  ^ 1.

"The canonical form of v, d containers deep: a scalar's, or, for a container,
 a frame pushed on aStack (an OrderedCollection, or nil for the first value)
 whose items the walk of canonical: makes canonical in turn."
PBCodec class >> _canonicalOpen: v depth: d on: aStack
  | frame kind items inner result |
  v isClassObject ifFalse: [
    (v isKindOf: PBTuple) ifTrue: [kind := #tuple. inner := d + 2. items := self _field: 'items' of: v base: _PBSequence].
    (kind isNil and: [v isKindOf: PBFrozenList]) ifTrue: [
      kind := #list. inner := d + 1. items := self _field: 'items' of: v base: _PBSequence].
    (kind isNil and: [(v isKindOf: Array) or: [v isKindOf: OrderedCollection]]) ifTrue: [
      kind := #array. inner := d + 1. items := v asArray].
    (kind isNil and: [v isKindOf: PBFrozenDict]) ifTrue: [
      kind := #map.
      inner := (self _field: 'keys' of: v base: PBFrozenDict) isEmpty ifTrue: [d + 2] ifFalse: [d + 3].
      items := self _interleave: (self _field: 'keys' of: v base: PBFrozenDict)
        with: (self _field: 'values' of: v base: PBFrozenDict)]].
  kind isNil ifTrue: [
    result := self _canonicalLeaf: v.
    d + (self _leafContainers: result) > self maxValueDepth ifTrue: [^ self _tooDeep].
    ^ result].
  inner > self maxValueDepth ifTrue: [^ self _tooDeep].
  frame := _PBValueFrame kind: kind source: v items: items depth: inner.
  aStack isNil ifFalse: [aStack addLast: frame].
  ^ frame.

"k1 v1 k2 v2 ...: the keys and values of a map, in its order."
PBCodec class >> _interleave: keys with: values
  | out |
  out := Array new: keys size * 2.
  1 to: keys size do: [:i |
    out at: 2 * i - 1 put: (keys at: i).
    out at: 2 * i put: (values at: i)].
  ^ out.

"The canonical container of a frame whose items are all canonical: the source
 itself when it was canonical already (same class, the same item objects)."
PBCodec class >> _canonicalClose: aFrame
  | kind v items results same |
  kind := aFrame kind.
  v := aFrame source.
  results := aFrame results.
  kind == #array ifTrue: [^ PBFrozenList withAll: results].
  items := aFrame items.
  same := true.
  1 to: results size do: [:i | (results at: i) == (items at: i) ifFalse: [same := false]].
  kind == #map ifTrue: [
    | pairs |
    same := same and: [v class == PBFrozenDict].
    pairs := (1 to: results size // 2) asArray collect: [:i | (results at: 2 * i - 1) -> (results at: 2 * i)].
    "The writer's map-key rule (format spec 'Map keys', PBKeys): a key that can
     never be a map key, and two keys that conflict (1 and 1.0, two NaNs of one
     encoding), signal PBValidationError. A PBFrozenDict was built under the
     reader's rule, which keeps NaN keys of one encoding apart."
    PBKeys checkMapKeys: (pairs collect: [:each | each key]) reading: false.
    same ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ PBFrozenDict withAssociations: pairs].
  kind == #tuple ifTrue: [
    (same and: [v class == PBTuple]) ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ PBTuple withAll: results].
  (same and: [v class == PBFrozenList]) ifTrue: [^ v].
  ^ PBFrozenList withAll: results.

"The canonical form of the scalar v (anything canonical:'s walk does not
 open as a container)."
PBCodec class >> _canonicalLeaf: v
  v isNil ifTrue: [^ v].
  (v == true or: [v == false]) ifTrue: [^ v].
  v isClassObject ifTrue: [^ self _refuse: v because: 'a class is not a value'].
  v isInteger ifTrue: [^ v].
  v isFloat ifTrue: [^ v].
  v isSymbol ifTrue: [
    ^ self _refuse: v because: 'the @sym kind is reserved and not part of format 4 (Spec 4.4); store a String'].
  v isString ifTrue: [^ self _checkUTF8: v].
  (v isKindOf: ByteArray) ifTrue: [
    ^ v class == ByteArray ifTrue: [v] ifFalse: [self _plainBytes: v]].
  (v isKindOf: Decimal) ifTrue: [^ self _canonicalDecimal: v].
  (v isKindOf: PBLegacyZoneDateTime) ifTrue: [
    ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: the format-3 zone datetime ' , v printString
      , ' cannot be written: its UTC instant needs the time-zone database of ' , v zone key
      , ' (Spec 4.3); store its UTC or fixed-offset form'].
  (v isKindOf: DateTime) ifTrue: [^ self _canonicalDateTime: v].
  (v isKindOf: CalendarDate) ifTrue: [
    v class == CalendarDate ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ CalendarDate year: (self _field: 'year' of: v base: CalendarDate)
        month: (self _field: 'month' of: v base: CalendarDate)
        day: (self _field: 'day' of: v base: CalendarDate)].
  (v isKindOf: TimeOfDay) ifTrue: [^ self _canonicalTime: v].
  (v isKindOf: TimeSpan) ifTrue: [
    v class == TimeSpan ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ TimeSpan microseconds: (self _field: 'total' of: v base: TimeSpan)].
  (v isKindOf: UUID) ifTrue: [
    v class == UUID ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ UUID fromBytes: (self _uuidBytes: v)].
  v == PBMissing default ifTrue: [^ v].
  (v isKindOf: PBMutableObject) ifTrue: [
    self _checkUTF8: (self _field: 'cellName' of: v base: PBMutableObject).
    v class == PBMutableObject ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ PBMutableObject name: (self _field: 'cellName' of: v base: PBMutableObject)].
  (v isKindOf: Dictionary) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _refuse: v because: 'its order is unspecified, and the order is part of the bytes; use PBFrozenDict'].
  (self _isReference: v) ifTrue: [
    ((v respondsTo: #tag) and: [v tag isString]) ifTrue: [self _checkUTF8: v tag].
    ^ v].
  ^ self _refuse: v because: 'it is not a canonical value of format 4'.

PBCodec class >> _refuse: v because: aString
  ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: a ' , v class name , ' cannot be stored ('
    , (self _preview: v) , '): ' , aString.

"aString, unless it holds a lone surrogate, which UTF-8 cannot encode."
PBCodec class >> _checkUTF8: aString
  aString do: [:ch |
    (ch asInteger between: 16rD800 and: 16rDFFF) ifTrue: [
      ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: a String holding the lone surrogate U+'
        , (ch asInteger printString: 16) , ' cannot be stored: strings in the format are valid UTF-8']].
  ^ aString.

PBCodec class >> _isReference: v
  ^ v isClassObject not and: [(v respondsTo: #isPBReference) and: [v isPBReference == true]].

"The instance variable aName of v as aBaseClass declares it: a subclass's
 accessors are never used to read the base value."
PBCodec class >> _field: aName of: v base: aBaseClass
  ^ v instVarAt: (aBaseClass allInstVarNames indexOf: aName).

"The 16 bytes of a UUID, read from UUID's own instance variable, never through
 a subclass's methods (codec, keys and notation all read them here)."
PBCodec class >> _uuidBytes: aUUID
  ^ self _field: 'bytes' of: aUUID base: UUID.

PBCodec class >> _plainBytes: aByteArray
  ^ ByteArray withAll: ((1 to: aByteArray size) asArray collect: [:i | aByteArray at: i]).

PBCodec class >> _canonicalDecimal: v
  | d kind |
  d := v.
  v class == Decimal ifFalse: [
    kind := self _field: 'kind' of: v base: Decimal.
    d := kind == #finite
      ifTrue: [Decimal sign: (self _field: 'sign' of: v base: Decimal)
        coefficient: (self _field: 'coefficient' of: v base: Decimal)
        exponent: (self _field: 'exponent' of: v base: Decimal)]
      ifFalse: [kind == #infinite
        ifTrue: [Decimal infinity: (self _field: 'sign' of: v base: Decimal)]
        ifFalse: [Decimal nan: (self _field: 'coefficient' of: v base: Decimal)
          signaling: kind == #snan sign: (self _field: 'sign' of: v base: Decimal)]]].
  (self _isDecimalInRange: d) ifFalse: [
    ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: the decimal ' , (self _preview: d)
      , ' has an exponent outside what CPython''s decimal module can represent'].
  ^ d.

"False for a finite decimal whose exponent is below MIN_ETINY or whose
 adjusted exponent is above MAX_EMAX: CPython refuses its text."
PBCodec class >> _isDecimalInRange: aDecimal
  | digits |
  aDecimal isFinite ifFalse: [^ true].
  aDecimal exponent < self _decimalMinExponent ifTrue: [^ false].
  digits := aDecimal coefficient printString size.
  ^ aDecimal exponent + digits - 1 <= self _decimalMaxAdjusted.

PBCodec class >> _canonicalZone: z
  z isNil ifTrue: [^ nil].
  (z isKindOf: ZoneOffset) ifTrue: [
    self _checkUTF8: (self _field: 'name' of: z base: ZoneOffset).
    z class == ZoneOffset ifTrue: [^ z].
    ^ ZoneOffset microseconds: (self _field: 'microseconds' of: z base: ZoneOffset)
        name: (self _field: 'name' of: z base: ZoneOffset)].
  (z isKindOf: ZoneName) ifTrue: [
    | key |
    key := self _field: 'key' of: z base: ZoneName.
    (PBZoneKeys includes: key) ifFalse: [
      ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: unknown time zone key ' , key printString].
    z class == ZoneName ifTrue: [^ z].
    ^ ZoneName key: key].
  ^ self _refuse: z because: 'it is not a time zone of format 4'.

PBCodec class >> _canonicalTime: v
  | zone |
  zone := self _canonicalZone: (self _field: 'zone' of: v base: TimeOfDay).
  (v class == TimeOfDay and: [zone == v zone]) ifTrue: [^ v].
  ^ TimeOfDay hour: (self _field: 'hour' of: v base: TimeOfDay)
      minute: (self _field: 'minute' of: v base: TimeOfDay)
      second: (self _field: 'second' of: v base: TimeOfDay)
      microsecond: (self _field: 'microsecond' of: v base: TimeOfDay)
      fold: (self _field: 'fold' of: v base: TimeOfDay)
      zone: zone.

PBCodec class >> _canonicalDateTime: v
  | zone f result |
  zone := self _canonicalZone: (self _field: 'zone' of: v base: DateTime).
  f := [:name | self _field: name of: v base: DateTime].
  result := (v class == DateTime and: [zone == v zone])
    ifTrue: [v]
    ifFalse: [(zone isKindOf: ZoneName)
      ifTrue: [DateTime
        utcFields: { f value: 'year'. f value: 'month'. f value: 'day'. f value: 'hour'.
          f value: 'minute'. f value: 'second'. f value: 'microsecond' }
        zoneName: zone]
      ifFalse: [DateTime year: (f value: 'year') month: (f value: 'month') day: (f value: 'day')
        hour: (f value: 'hour') minute: (f value: 'minute') second: (f value: 'second')
        microsecond: (f value: 'microsecond') fold: (f value: 'fold') zone: zone]].
  result isInstantForm ifTrue: [self _checkInstantBand: result].
  ^ result.

"Signals PBNotSupportedError when the wall clock of an instant-form DateTime
 could fall outside years 1 to 9999 in its zone: deciding needs the zone's
 rules (format spec, ['instant', key]), and ProtoBase refuses to read such a
 value back. Writing only: a reader presents the instant in UTC."
PBCodec class >> _checkInstantBand: aDateTime
  | utc |
  utc := aDateTime utcOrdinalMicroseconds.
  (utc < self _instantLow or: [utc > self _instantHigh]) ifTrue: [
    ^ PBNotSupportedError signal: 'PBCodec: the instant ' , aDateTime printString
      , ' lies within one day of year 1 or year 9999, so its wall clock in '
      , aDateTime zone key , ' may fall outside years 1 to 9999; protoBaseST has no time-zone database to decide (Spec 4.3)'].
  ^ aDateTime.

"=== encoding ================================================================="

"The wire form of aValue (canonicalized first): msgpack-ready data where
 every map is a MessagePackMap. aBlock value: anAtom answers the wire form of
 a reference to it; PBCodec pointerRef and PBCodec tokenRef are the two
 standard blocks."
PBCodec class >> toWire: aValue atomRef: aBlock
  ^ self _wire: (self canonical: aValue) ref: aBlock.

"As toWire:atomRef:, with a PBValidationError of the codec's own naming
 aHolder (canonical:for:)."
PBCodec class >> toWire: aValue atomRef: aBlock for: aHolder
  ^ self _wire: (self canonical: aValue for: aHolder) ref: aBlock.

"The wire form of aValue, an attribute value of a record being saved, as
 toWire:atomRef:for: answers it, refusing what it refuses with the same text.
 The values every writer may write as they are, whatever their origin, are
 answered first: nil, a Boolean, an integer msgpack holds, a float, an atom of
 a registered class (its tag is its class's registered name). Every other
 value goes through canonical:for:, so a value a reader accepts but a writer
 must refuse (a format-3 zone datetime, an instant within a day of year 1 or
 9999, a container deeper than the writer's limit, map keys only the reader's
 legacy rule admits, a string holding a lone surrogate) is refused here, even
 when it was copied forward from a decoded record (PBObject >> withAll:, a
 tree node rebuilt around a stored value): a decoded value is not writable by
 construction."
PBCodec class >> wireOf: aValue atomRef: aBlock for: aHolder
  aValue isNil ifTrue: [^ aValue].
  (aValue == true or: [aValue == false]) ifTrue: [^ aValue].
  (aValue isInteger and: [aValue between: self _intMin and: self _intMax]) ifTrue: [^ aValue].
  aValue isFloat ifTrue: [^ aValue].
  ((aValue isKindOf: PBAtom) and: [aValue class ~~ PBOpaqueAtom and: [aValue isPBReference == true]]) ifTrue: [
    ^ aBlock value: aValue].
  ^ self toWire: aValue atomRef: aBlock for: aHolder.

"The block that writes a reference as its pointer: {'@ref': [segment, offset,
 tag]}, from the reference's pointer and tag."
PBCodec class >> pointerRef
  ^ [:anAtom | self _pointerRefOf: anAtom].

"The block of exact tokens: every reference writes {'@ref': nil}."
PBCodec class >> tokenRef
  ^ [:anAtom | self _tagged: '@ref' body: nil].

PBCodec class >> _pointerRefOf: anAtom
  | ptr |
  ptr := anAtom pointer.
  ptr isNil ifTrue: [
    ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec: ' , anAtom printString , ' is not saved: it has no pointer to refer to'].
  "The canonical spelling (format spec, 'The name a writer puts in a reference'),
   whatever was registered when the reference was read; a name every reader
   refuses is PBValidationError."
  ^ self _tagged: '@ref' body: { ptr segmentBytes. ptr offset. PBTypeRegistry writerTag: anAtom tag }.

PBCodec class >> _tagged: aTag body: aBody
  ^ MessagePackMap withAll: { aTag -> aBody }.

"The wire form of the canonical value aValue, built with an explicit stack."
PBCodec class >> _wire: aValue ref: aBlock
  | stack result |
  result := self _wireOpen: aValue ref: aBlock on: nil.
  (result isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [^ result].
  stack := OrderedCollection with: result.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | frame r |
    frame := stack last.
    frame atEnd
      ifTrue: [
        stack removeLast.
        r := self _wireClose: frame]
      ifFalse: [r := self _wireOpen: frame next ref: aBlock on: stack].
    (r isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [
      stack isEmpty ifTrue: [result := r] ifFalse: [stack last add: r]]].
  ^ result.

"The wire form of the canonical scalar v, or, for a container, a frame pushed
 on aStack (nil for the first value)."
PBCodec class >> _wireOpen: v ref: aBlock on: aStack
  | frame |
  (v isKindOf: _PBSequence) ifTrue: [
    frame := _PBValueFrame kind: ((v isKindOf: PBTuple) ifTrue: [#tuple] ifFalse: [#list])
      source: v items: (self _field: 'items' of: v base: _PBSequence) depth: 0].
  (v isKindOf: PBFrozenDict) ifTrue: [
    frame := _PBValueFrame kind: #map source: v
      items: (self _interleave: (self _field: 'keys' of: v base: PBFrozenDict)
        with: (self _field: 'values' of: v base: PBFrozenDict))
      depth: 0].
  frame isNil ifTrue: [^ self _wireLeaf: v ref: aBlock].
  aStack isNil ifFalse: [aStack addLast: frame].
  ^ frame.

PBCodec class >> _wireClose: aFrame
  | results |
  results := aFrame results.
  aFrame kind == #list ifTrue: [^ results].
  aFrame kind == #tuple ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@tup' body: results].
  ^ self _tagged: '@map' body: ((1 to: results size // 2) asArray collect: [:i |
    { results at: 2 * i - 1. results at: 2 * i }]).

PBCodec class >> _wireLeaf: v ref: aBlock
  v isNil ifTrue: [^ v].
  (v == true or: [v == false]) ifTrue: [^ v].
  v isInteger ifTrue: [
    (v between: self _intMin and: self _intMax) ifTrue: [^ v].
    ^ self _tagged: '@int' body: (v printString: 16) asLowercase].
  v isFloat ifTrue: [^ v].
  v isString ifTrue: [^ v].
  (v isKindOf: ByteArray) ifTrue: [^ v].
  (v isKindOf: Decimal) ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@dec' body: v printString].
  (v isKindOf: DateTime) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _tagged: '@dt' body: {
      v year. v month. v day. v hour. v minute. v second. v microsecond. v fold.
      v isInstantForm ifTrue: [{ 'instant'. v zone key }] ifFalse: [self _wireZone: v zone] }].
  (v isKindOf: CalendarDate) ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@date' body: { v year. v month. v day }].
  (v isKindOf: TimeOfDay) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _tagged: '@time' body: {
      v hour. v minute. v second. v microsecond. v fold. self _wireZone: v zone }].
  (v isKindOf: TimeSpan) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _tagged: '@td' body: { v days. v seconds. v microseconds }].
  (v isKindOf: UUID) ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@uuid' body: (self _uuidBytes: v)].
  v == PBMissing default ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@missing' body: 0].
  (v isKindOf: PBMutableObject) ifTrue: [^ self _tagged: '@mut' body: v name].
  (self _isReference: v) ifTrue: [^ aBlock value: v].
  ^ PBUnexpectedError signal: 'PBCodec: no wire form for a canonical ' , v class name.

PBCodec class >> _wireZone: z
  z isNil ifTrue: [^ nil].
  (z isKindOf: ZoneOffset) ifTrue: [^ { 'fixed'. z microseconds. z name }].
  ^ { 'zone'. z key }.

"The msgpack bytes of aValue; references are written as their pointers."
PBCodec class >> encode: aValue
  ^ MessagePack encode: (self toWire: aValue atomRef: self pointerRef).

"=== decoding ================================================================="

"The value aByteArray holds (one value, as it sits in a state map);
 references decode to PBUnresolvedRef. Malformed bytes signal
 PBCorruptionError."
PBCodec class >> decode: aByteArray
  | tree |
  (aByteArray isKindOf: ByteArray) ifFalse: [
    ^ PBValidationError signal: 'PBCodec decode: a ByteArray was expected, not a ' , aByteArray class name].
  tree := [MessagePack decodeOrdered: aByteArray strictKeys: false]
    on: Error do: [:e |
      (e isKindOf: MessageNotUnderstood) ifTrue: [e pass].
      (e isKindOf: MessagePackDepthExceeded) ifTrue: [self tooDeepData: 'PBCodec'].
      PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: malformed msgpack: ' , e messageText].
  ^ self fromWire: tree resolver: nil.

"The value of aTree, as MessagePack decodeOrdered:strictKeys: answers it. A
 reference is aResolver refTo: segmentBytes offset: anInteger tag: aTag, or a
 PBUnresolvedRef when aResolver is nil. Data nested deeper than maxValueDepth
 containers is PBCorruptionError. The walk keeps an explicit stack, and meets
 references and map keys in the order of the data: a key is checked, and its
 atoms loaded, before its value is read."
"As fromWire:resolver:, answering first the wire data that is its own value,
 as _fromWireOpen:depth:resolver:on: answers it (same order of tests): nil, an
 integer, a string, a float, a Boolean. The attribute values of a record."
PBCodec class >> fromWireValue: aTree resolver: aResolver
  aTree isNil ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  aTree isInteger ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree isString and: [aTree isSymbol not]) ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  aTree isFloat ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree == true or: [aTree == false]) ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  ^ self fromWire: aTree resolver: aResolver.

PBCodec class >> fromWire: aTree resolver: aResolver
  | stack result |
  result := self _fromWireOpen: aTree depth: 0 resolver: aResolver on: nil.
  (result isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [^ result].
  stack := OrderedCollection with: result.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | frame r |
    frame := stack last.
    frame atEnd
      ifTrue: [
        stack removeLast.
        r := self _fromWireClose: frame]
      ifFalse: [r := self _fromWireOpen: frame next depth: frame depth resolver: aResolver on: stack].
    (r isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [
      stack isEmpty
        ifTrue: [result := r]
        ifFalse: [self _fromWireAdd: r to: stack last resolver: aResolver]]].
  ^ result.

"The value of the wire data aTree, d containers deep: a scalar's, or, for a
 list, a @tup or a @map, a frame pushed on aStack (nil for the first value)."
PBCodec class >> _fromWireOpen: aTree depth: d resolver: aResolver on: aStack
  | frame |
  aTree isNil ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree == true or: [aTree == false]) ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  aTree isInteger ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  aTree isFloat ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree isString and: [aTree isSymbol not]) ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree isKindOf: ByteArray) ifTrue: [^ aTree].
  (aTree isKindOf: Array) ifTrue: [
    d + 1 > self maxValueDepth ifTrue: [^ self _tooDeepData].
    frame := _PBValueFrame kind: #list source: aTree items: aTree depth: d + 1].
  (aTree isKindOf: MessagePackMap) ifTrue: [
    frame := self _fromTagged: aTree depth: d resolver: aResolver.
    (frame isKindOf: _PBValueFrame) ifFalse: [^ frame]].
  (aTree isKindOf: MessagePackExt) ifTrue: [
    ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: a msgpack ext value (type ' , aTree type printString
      , ') is never a canonical value'].
  frame isNil ifTrue: [^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: malformed encoded value: ' , (self _preview: aTree)].
  aStack isNil ifFalse: [aStack addLast: frame].
  ^ frame.

"aResult, the value of an item of aFrame, added to it. A map key is checked
 against the reader's map-key rule and its atoms loaded before the value that
 follows it is read."
PBCodec class >> _fromWireAdd: aResult to: aFrame resolver: aResolver
  | reason |
  aFrame add: aResult.
  (aFrame kind == #map and: [aFrame position odd]) ifFalse: [^ self].
  reason := PBKeys _unkeyableReason: aResult legacyAllowed: true.
  reason isNil ifFalse: [^ self _corrupt: '@map' body: aFrame source because: reason].
  self _loadKeyAtoms: aResult resolver: aResolver.

PBCodec class >> _fromWireClose: aFrame
  | results pairs |
  results := aFrame results.
  aFrame kind == #list ifTrue: [^ PBFrozenList withAll: results].
  aFrame kind == #tuple ifTrue: [^ PBTuple withAll: results].
  pairs := (1 to: results size // 2) asArray collect: [:i | (results at: 2 * i - 1) -> (results at: 2 * i)].
  "The reader's map-key rule (PBKeys checkMapKeys:reading: true) is the rule
   PBFrozenDict withAssociations: builds under: conflicting keys are
   PBValidationError, read as corruption; NaN keys of one encoding (format 3)
   stay two keys."
  ^ [PBFrozenDict withAssociations: pairs] on: PBValidationError do: [:e |
    self _corrupt: '@map' body: aFrame source because: e messageText].

"The value of a tagged map d containers deep, or, for @tup and @map, the frame
 of its items (not yet pushed)."
PBCodec class >> _fromTagged: aMap depth: d resolver: aResolver
  | assoc tag body |
  aMap size = 1 ifFalse: [
    ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: a tagged value is a map with exactly one key, not '
      , aMap size printString , ': ' , (self _preview: aMap)].
  assoc := aMap associations first.
  tag := assoc key.
  body := assoc value.
  (tag isString and: [tag isSymbol not]) ifFalse: [
    ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: a map key must be a string, not ' , (self _preview: tag)].
  tag = '@tup' ifTrue: [
    (body isKindOf: Array) ifFalse: [^ self _corrupt: tag body: body because: 'an array was expected'].
    d + 2 > self maxValueDepth ifTrue: [^ self _tooDeepData].
    ^ _PBValueFrame kind: #tuple source: body items: body depth: d + 2].
  tag = '@map' ifTrue: [^ self _mapFrame: body depth: d].
  (d + 3 > self maxValueDepth and: [d + (self _wireTreeDepth: aMap) > self maxValueDepth]) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _tooDeepData].
  tag = '@int' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeInt: body].
  tag = '@dec' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeDecimal: body].
  tag = '@date' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeDate: body].
  tag = '@time' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeTime: body].
  tag = '@dt' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeDateTime: body].
  tag = '@td' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeTimeSpan: body].
  tag = '@uuid' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeUUID: body].
  tag = '@missing' ifTrue: [
    (body isInteger and: [body = 0]) ifFalse: [^ self _corrupt: tag body: body because: 'the body must be the integer 0'].
    ^ PBMissing default].
  tag = '@ref' ifTrue: [^ self _decodeRef: body resolver: aResolver].
  tag = '@mut' ifTrue: [
    (body isString and: [body notEmpty]) ifFalse: [
      ^ self _corrupt: tag body: body because: 'a non-empty name was expected'].
    ^ PBMutableObject name: body].
  ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: unknown codec tag ' , (self _preview: tag).

"The frame of a @map body d containers deep: its keys and values interleaved,
 after every entry is checked to be a [key, value] array."
PBCodec class >> _mapFrame: aBody depth: d
  | items inner |
  (aBody isKindOf: Array) ifFalse: [^ self _corrupt: '@map' body: aBody because: 'an array was expected'].
  items := Array new: aBody size * 2.
  1 to: aBody size do: [:i |
    | pair |
    pair := aBody at: i.
    ((pair isKindOf: Array) and: [pair size = 2]) ifFalse: [
      ^ self _corrupt: '@map' body: aBody because: 'each entry is a [key, value] array'].
    items at: 2 * i - 1 put: (pair at: 1).
    items at: 2 * i put: (pair at: 2)].
  inner := aBody isEmpty ifTrue: [d + 2] ifFalse: [d + 3].
  inner > self maxValueDepth ifTrue: [^ self _tooDeepData].
  ^ _PBValueFrame kind: #map source: aBody items: items depth: inner.

"The msgpack containers (arrays and maps, an empty one included) the wire data
 aTree nests, counted with an explicit stack."
PBCodec class >> _wireTreeDepth: aTree
  | stack best |
  best := 0.
  stack := OrderedCollection with: aTree -> 0.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | entry t d |
    entry := stack removeLast.
    t := entry key.
    d := entry value.
    (t isKindOf: Array)
      ifTrue: [
        d := d + 1.
        1 to: t size do: [:i | stack addLast: (t at: i) -> d]]
      ifFalse: [(t isKindOf: MessagePackMap) ifTrue: [
        d := d + 1.
        t associations do: [:each | stack addLast: each key -> d; addLast: each value -> d]]].
    d > best ifTrue: [best := d]].
  ^ best.

PBCodec class >> _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: aString
  ^ PBCorruptionError signal: 'PBCodec: malformed ' , aTag , ' value ' , (self _preview: aBody)
    , ': ' , aString.

"aBlock's value; an Error of a value constructor (not a PBDBError, not a
 MessageNotUnderstood) is a malformed body."
PBCodec class >> _build: aBlock tag: aTag body: aBody
  ^ aBlock on: Error do: [:e |
    ((e isKindOf: PBDBError) or: [e isKindOf: MessageNotUnderstood]) ifTrue: [e pass].
    self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: e messageText].

PBCodec class >> _preview: anObject
  | text |
  text := [anObject printString] on: Error do: [:e | 'a ' , anObject class name].
  ^ text size <= 80 ifTrue: [text] ifFalse: [(text copyFrom: 1 to: 77) , '...'].

"aBody when it is an Array of n items whose first aCount items are Integers;
 otherwise a corruption."
PBCodec class >> _fields: aBody count: n integers: aCount tag: aTag
  ((aBody isKindOf: Array) and: [aBody size = n]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: 'an array of ' , n printString , ' items was expected'].
  1 to: aCount do: [:i |
    (aBody at: i) isInteger ifFalse: [
      ^ self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: 'item ' , i printString , ' must be an integer']].
  ^ aBody.

PBCodec class >> _decodeInt: aBody
  | value |
  value := self _parseHex: aBody.
  value isNil ifTrue: [^ self _corrupt: '@int' body: aBody because: 'not signed lowercase hexadecimal without leading zeros'].
  (value between: self _intMin and: self _intMax) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@int' body: aBody because: 'an integer in the native range is never @int'].
  ^ value.

"The Integer of a canonical @int text ('-' then lowercase hexadecimal digits,
 the first not 0), or nil."
PBCodec class >> _parseHex: aText
  | start value |
  (aText isString and: [aText isSymbol not and: [aText notEmpty]]) ifFalse: [^ nil].
  start := aText first = $- ifTrue: [2] ifFalse: [1].
  start > aText size ifTrue: [^ nil].
  (aText at: start) = $0 ifTrue: [^ nil].
  value := 0.
  start to: aText size do: [:i |
    | c |
    c := (aText at: i) asInteger.
    (c between: 48 and: 57)
      ifTrue: [value := value * 16 + (c - 48)]
      ifFalse: [(c between: 97 and: 102)
        ifTrue: [value := value * 16 + (c - 87)]
        ifFalse: [^ nil]]].
  ^ start = 2 ifTrue: [value negated] ifFalse: [value].

PBCodec class >> _decodeDecimal: aBody
  | d |
  (aBody isString and: [aBody isSymbol not]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@dec' body: aBody because: 'a string was expected'].
  d := self _build: [Decimal fromString: aBody] tag: '@dec' body: aBody.
  d printString = aBody ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@dec' body: aBody because: 'not the canonical text (the to-scientific-string form)'].
  (self _isDecimalInRange: d) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@dec' body: aBody because: 'an exponent CPython''s decimal module cannot represent'].
  ^ d.

PBCodec class >> _decodeDate: aBody
  | f |
  f := self _fields: aBody count: 3 integers: 3 tag: '@date'.
  ^ self _build: [CalendarDate year: (f at: 1) month: (f at: 2) day: (f at: 3)] tag: '@date' body: aBody.

"The zone of a tz field: nil, ['fixed', offset, name] or ['zone', key]. The
 instant form is read by _decodeDateTime: itself; in a @time it is malformed."
PBCodec class >> _decodeZone: tz tag: aTag body: aBody
  | kind |
  tz isNil ifTrue: [^ nil].
  ((tz isKindOf: Array) and: [tz notEmpty and: [(tz at: 1) isString]]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: 'malformed tzinfo'].
  kind := tz at: 1.
  (kind = 'fixed' and: [tz size = 3 and: [(tz at: 2) isInteger and: [(tz at: 3) isString]]]) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _build: [ZoneOffset microseconds: (tz at: 2) name: (tz at: 3)] tag: aTag body: aBody].
  (kind = 'zone' and: [tz size = 2 and: [(tz at: 2) isString]]) ifTrue: [
    ^ self _zoneName: (tz at: 2) tag: aTag body: aBody].
  ^ self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: 'malformed tzinfo'.

PBCodec class >> _zoneName: aKey tag: aTag body: aBody
  (PBZoneKeys includes: aKey) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: aTag body: aBody because: 'unknown time zone key ' , aKey printString].
  ^ ZoneName key: aKey.

PBCodec class >> _decodeTime: aBody
  | f zone |
  f := self _fields: aBody count: 6 integers: 5 tag: '@time'.
  zone := self _decodeZone: (f at: 6) tag: '@time' body: aBody.
  ^ self _build: [TimeOfDay hour: (f at: 1) minute: (f at: 2) second: (f at: 3)
      microsecond: (f at: 4) fold: (f at: 5) zone: zone] tag: '@time' body: aBody.

PBCodec class >> _decodeDateTime: aBody
  | f tz fields zone |
  f := self _fields: aBody count: 9 integers: 8 tag: '@dt'.
  tz := f at: 9.
  fields := f copyFrom: 1 to: 7.
  ((tz isKindOf: Array) and: [tz size = 2 and: [(tz at: 1) = 'instant' and: [(tz at: 2) isString]]])
    ifTrue: [
      (f at: 8) = 0 ifFalse: [^ self _corrupt: '@dt' body: aBody because: 'an instant has fold 0'].
      zone := self _zoneName: (tz at: 2) tag: '@dt' body: aBody.
      ^ self _build: [DateTime utcFields: fields zoneName: zone] tag: '@dt' body: aBody].
  ((tz isKindOf: Array) and: [tz size = 2 and: [(tz at: 1) = 'zone' and: [(tz at: 2) isString]]])
    ifTrue: [
      zone := self _zoneName: (tz at: 2) tag: '@dt' body: aBody.
      ^ self _build: [PBLegacyZoneDateTime wallClockFields: fields fold: (f at: 8) zoneName: zone]
          tag: '@dt' body: aBody].
  zone := self _decodeZone: tz tag: '@dt' body: aBody.
  ^ self _build: [DateTime year: (f at: 1) month: (f at: 2) day: (f at: 3) hour: (f at: 4)
      minute: (f at: 5) second: (f at: 6) microsecond: (f at: 7) fold: (f at: 8) zone: zone]
    tag: '@dt' body: aBody.

PBCodec class >> _decodeTimeSpan: aBody
  | f |
  f := self _fields: aBody count: 3 integers: 3 tag: '@td'.
  (((f at: 2) between: 0 and: 86399) and: [(f at: 3) between: 0 and: 999999]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@td' body: aBody
      because: 'not normalized: 0 <= seconds < 86400 and 0 <= microseconds < 10^6'].
  ^ self _build: [TimeSpan days: (f at: 1) seconds: (f at: 2) microseconds: (f at: 3)]
    tag: '@td' body: aBody.

PBCodec class >> _decodeUUID: aBody
  ((aBody isKindOf: ByteArray) and: [aBody size = 16]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@uuid' body: aBody because: '16 bytes were expected'].
  ^ UUID fromBytes: aBody.

"A key is identified by its oid: the atoms of the key k (an atom, or atoms in
 a tuple) are loaded now through a resolver that loads keys
 (_PBLoadResolver >> loadKey:, which refuses a record already being decoded).
 A resolver without loadKey: (only tests that call fromWire:resolver: with a
 plain storage) leaves the key atoms as stubs: a record whose key refers back
 to itself is still refused with PBCorruptionError, one level later, when the
 stub is loaded, so the recursion always ends."
PBCodec class >> _loadKeyAtoms: k resolver: aResolver
  | stack |
  (aResolver isNil or: [(aResolver respondsTo: #loadKey:) not]) ifTrue: [^ self].
  "Depth first, in the key's order, with an explicit stack."
  stack := OrderedCollection with: k.
  [stack isEmpty] whileFalse: [
    | each |
    each := stack removeLast.
    (each isKindOf: PBAtom) ifTrue: [aResolver loadKey: each].
    (each isKindOf: PBTuple) ifTrue: [each asArray reverseDo: [:item | stack addLast: item]]].

PBCodec class >> _decodeRef: aBody resolver: aResolver
  | f segment offset tag bytes |
  f := self _fields: aBody count: 3 integers: 0 tag: '@ref'.
  segment := f at: 1.
  offset := f at: 2.
  tag := f at: 3.
  bytes := ((segment isKindOf: ByteArray) and: [segment size = 16])
    ifTrue: [segment]
    ifFalse: [self _segmentFromHex: segment].
  bytes isNil ifTrue: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@ref' body: aBody because: 'the segment is 16 bytes (or, in format 2, 32 hexadecimal digits)'].
  (offset isInteger and: [offset >= 0]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@ref' body: aBody because: 'the offset is an integer >= 0'].
  ((tag isInteger and: [tag between: 0 and: PBTypeRegistry builtinCount - 1])
      or: [tag isString and: [tag isSymbol not and: [tag notEmpty]]]) ifFalse: [
    ^ self _corrupt: '@ref' body: aBody because: 'the type tag is an alias of the table or a type name'].
  "The name a writer would put: a built-in name (format 2) becomes its alias, an
   application alias the declared name of its registered class (format spec, Type names)."
  tag := PBTypeRegistry canonicalTag: tag.
  aResolver isNil ifTrue: [
    ^ PBUnresolvedRef pointer: (PBAtomPointer segment: bytes offset: offset) tag: tag].
  ^ aResolver refTo: bytes offset: offset tag: tag.

"The 16 bytes of a format-2 segment written as 32 hexadecimal digits, or nil."
PBCodec class >> _segmentFromHex: aText
  | bytes |
  ((aText isString and: [aText isSymbol not]) and: [aText size = 32]) ifFalse: [^ nil].
  bytes := (1 to: 16) asArray collect: [:i |
    | hi lo |
    hi := self _hexDigit: (aText at: 2 * i - 1).
    lo := self _hexDigit: (aText at: 2 * i).
    (hi isNil or: [lo isNil]) ifTrue: [^ nil].
    hi * 16 + lo].
  ^ ByteArray withAll: bytes.

PBCodec class >> _hexDigit: aCharacter
  | c |
  c := aCharacter asInteger.
  (c between: 48 and: 57) ifTrue: [^ c - 48].
  (c between: 97 and: 102) ifTrue: [^ c - 87].
  (c between: 65 and: 70) ifTrue: [^ c - 55].
  ^ nil.
